      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "Angle of a sector:",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "heading": "Stem and Leaf diagrams",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "Definition",
      "html": "<ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Stem-and-Leaf diagram is a quick way of summarizing a range of data.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>There is a column known as the stem, which contains unique\nelements of data formed by removing last digits of the data.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Keys are used in this diagram</p>\n</li>\n</ul>"
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "Structure",
      "html": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.znotes.org/cie/igcse/maths-0580/image072.png\"></p><ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">A key or legend is always included to show how to read the diagram.</li>\n</ul><p><strong>How to find the median of a Stem leaf diagram</strong></p><ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>First ensure the data is ordered from smallest to largest .</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Locate the middle value.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>If there's an odd number of data points, the median is the single middle value.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>If there's an even number of data points, the median is the average of the two middle values</p>\n</li>\n</ul>"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "heading": "Pictograms",
      "html": "<ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Data is represented in pictures</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>A key is given to represent the value of a picture.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>There are no axes</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Frequency is represented by symbols</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>A key shows value of 1 symbol</p>\n</li>\n</ul><p>E.g. <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.znotes.org/cie/igcse/maths-0580/image073.png\">\n= 5 people</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.znotes.org/cie/igcse/maths-0580/image074.png\"></p><p>Favorite Fast Food of 100 Children</p>"
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "heading": "Scatter Diagrams",
      "html": "<ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Displays the correlation between two sets of data</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>May have positive, negative or no correlation</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Scatter graphs are used to plot pairs of data</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>The vertical and horizontal axes represent the two quantities being measured</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Points are plotted as crosses, ×</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>The general shape formed by the points shows the type of correlation</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.znotes.org/cie/igcse/maths-0580/image075.png\"></p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<h3>Correlation</h3>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p><strong>Positive</strong>: Indicates a relationship between two variables where they tend to move in the same direction</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p><strong>Negative</strong>:  An inverse relationship between two variables, meaning as one variable increases, the other decreases</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p><strong>No Correlation:</strong> No derivable relationship between the two sets of data being plotted</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<h3>Line of Best Fit</h3>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Use a transparent ruler to visually estimate the trend of the data points</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Draw a straight line that represents that trend.</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Aim for roughly the same number of data points above and below the line</p>\n</li>\n</ul><img width=\"30%\">"
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "Correlation",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "level": "h3",
      "heading": "Line of Best Fit",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "level": "h2",
      "heading": "Bar Charts",
      "html": "<ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Used to represent discrete data (data in separate categories).</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Each bar represents a category and its frequency (or value).</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Bars must be of equal width and equally spaced</p>\n</li>\n</ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.znotes.org/allimages/4d989a27a15210d21a2691b3.webp\"></p><p><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Horizontal Axis shows categories</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Vertical axis shows frequency or measured value</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Height of Bar = Frequency</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Used when data is categorical and discrete</p>\n</li>\n</ul><p><strong>Reading a Bar Chart</strong></p><ul node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Look at the height of each bar</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Match it with the scale on the y-axis</p>\n</li>\n<li node=\"[object Object]\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 2px 0px;\">\n<p>Compare bars to see the highest, lowest, or differences</p>\n</li>\n</ul>"
    }
  ]
}